use ../../cli

export cli-command Update:
    commandName: update
    description:
        Using the dependencies in the piton.config.pi, update all packages
    positionalArguments:
        packages:
            optional list of package names to update; if not provided, all
            packages will be updated
    namedArguments:
        force:
            Replace a package even when it was edited since it was installed,
            discarding the edits. Each package whose edits were discarded is
            named in a warning, with what changed in it.
        diff:
            Show every file each update changed, line by line, from what was on
            disk before to what is installed now, local edits included. Each
            changed region is printed with three lines of unchanged context,
            and every line with its old and new line number: an unchanged line
            has both, a removed line only its old one, an added line only its
            new one. Separate regions of one file are split by a line of its
            own. Each package says how many files changed, and says so when
            none did. When an update is refused because a package was edited,
            the diff shows those edits instead: the package as it was
            installed, fetched again from the commit the lock file records,
            against what is on disk now. The diff is computed by the compiler
            itself, so it needs no diff program installed. On a terminal removed lines are red and
            added lines green.
